WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.395
Job Hunting.

2
00:00:01.675 --> 00:00:05.558
Day 83 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the Career phase.

3
00:00:07.308 --> 00:00:08.332
The key idea.

4
00:00:08.612 --> 00:00:19.961
Today's goal: plan your job search, talk to recruiters with confidence, ask for referrals, follow up without being pushy, and handle offers, rejections and notice periods professionally.

5
00:00:21.311 --> 00:00:22.165
Part 1.

6
00:00:22.445 --> 00:00:23.938
The job-search pipeline.

7
00:00:25.188 --> 00:00:26.105
Step 1:

8
00:00:26.385 --> 00:00:27.175
Target:

9
00:00:27.455 --> 00:00:31.636
2 to 3 role types, preferred companies, salary range, location.

10
00:00:31.916 --> 00:00:32.833
Step 2:

11
00:00:33.113 --> 00:00:38.681
Prepare: resume, cover letter, LinkedIn, 6 to 8 STAR stories, a portfolio or GitHub.

12
00:00:38.961 --> 00:00:39.879
Step 3:

13
00:00:40.159 --> 00:00:43.807
Reach out: referrals first, then recruiters, then job portals.

14
00:00:44.087 --> 00:00:45.047
Step 4:

15
00:00:45.327 --> 00:00:48.505
Interview: screening, technical, managerial, HR.

16
00:00:48.785 --> 00:00:49.745
Step 5:

17
00:00:50.025 --> 00:00:53.567
Decide: compare offers, negotiate, accept, resign well.

18
00:00:54.917 --> 00:00:55.557
Tip:

19
00:00:55.837 --> 00:00:57.223
Referrals work best.

20
00:00:57.503 --> 00:01:03.925
Applications with a referral are usually far more likely to get an interview than cold applications on a portal.

21
00:01:04.205 --> 00:01:06.893
Spend most of your time on people, not portals.

22
00:01:08.243 --> 00:01:09.117
Part 2.

23
00:01:09.397 --> 00:01:10.357
Key words.

24
00:01:11.607 --> 00:01:12.973
Here is a quick table:

25
00:01:13.253 --> 00:01:26.437
Word or phrase, and Meaning. job description (JD) / requisition or job ID: the role details or its number. shortlisted or screening call: selected for the next step or first call.

26
00:01:26.717 --> 00:01:48.221
CTC or fixed or variable or in-hand: total cost to company or guaranteed or bonus or monthly take-home. notice period or buyout or last working day (LWD): time before you can join or paying to leave early or final day. offer letter or background verification (BGV): the written offer or checks of

27
00:01:48.501 --> 00:01:56.863
your history. counter-offer: your current company offers more to keep you. on hold or position closed: paused or no longer hiring.

28
00:01:58.213 --> 00:01:59.109
Part 3.

29
00:01:59.389 --> 00:02:00.883
The recruiter screening call.

30
00:02:02.133 --> 00:02:03.498
Here is a quick table:

31
00:02:03.778 --> 00:02:05.741
Recruiter asks, and Good answer.

32
00:02:06.021 --> 00:02:07.322
Tell me about yourself.:

33
00:02:07.602 --> 00:02:11.485
(60 seconds: present, then past, then future; see Interviews).

34
00:02:11.765 --> 00:02:13.450
Why are you looking for a change?:

35
00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:17.463
I'm looking for larger-scale systems and a path to a Staff role.

36
00:02:17.743 --> 00:02:19.301
What's your current CTC?:

37
00:02:19.581 --> 00:02:22.119
(In some places this question isn't allowed.

38
00:02:22.399 --> 00:02:25.258
You can say:) I'd prefer to focus on the role's range.

39
00:02:25.538 --> 00:02:29.101
My expectation is around 55 rupees, 60 lakh.

40
00:02:29.381 --> 00:02:31.087
What's your expected CTC?:

41
00:02:31.367 --> 00:02:37.405
Based on the market for this level, 55 rupees, 60 lakh, depending on the overall package.

42
00:02:37.685 --> 00:02:39.071
What's your notice period?:

43
00:02:39.351 --> 00:02:42.317
60 days, and it's negotiable to 45.

44
00:02:42.597 --> 00:02:44.261
I can also discuss a buyout.

45
00:02:44.541 --> 00:02:45.949
Do you have other offers?:

46
00:02:46.229 --> 00:02:48.426
I'm in the final rounds with two companies.

47
00:02:48.706 --> 00:02:50.349
(Only say this if it's true.).

48
00:02:51.699 --> 00:02:54.195
Are you open to relocation or office days?:

49
00:02:54.475 --> 00:02:58.037
Yes, Bengaluru works, and three office days a week is fine.

50
00:02:59.387 --> 00:03:00.305
Part 4.

51
00:03:00.585 --> 00:03:02.270
Questions to ask recruiters.

52
00:03:03.520 --> 00:03:05.803
What's the team and product I'd be working on?

53
00:03:06.083 --> 00:03:09.432
What does the interview process look like, and how long does it take?

54
00:03:09.712 --> 00:03:11.824
What's the budgeted range for this role?

55
00:03:12.104 --> 00:03:15.347
Why is the position open: new role or replacement?

56
00:03:15.627 --> 00:03:18.336
What's the work model: remote, hybrid, office?

57
00:03:18.616 --> 00:03:21.112
When can I expect to hear back after each round?

58
00:03:22.462 --> 00:03:23.422
Part 5.

59
00:03:23.702 --> 00:03:25.729
Following up (without being pushy).

60
00:03:26.979 --> 00:03:28.557
After applying (1 week).

61
00:03:28.837 --> 00:03:30.715
Here is a template you can copy.

62
00:03:30.995 --> 00:03:38.205
Hi Riya, I applied for the Senior Backend Engineer role (ID 4471) last Monday.

63
00:03:38.485 --> 00:03:41.579
I'm. very. interested in the payments platform team.

64
00:03:41.859 --> 00:03:43.949
Is there any update on the shortlisting?

65
00:03:44.229 --> 00:03:46.213
Happy to share anything else you need.

66
00:03:46.493 --> 00:03:47.261
Thanks!

67
00:03:50.111 --> 00:03:52.330
After an interview (24 hours).

68
00:03:52.610 --> 00:03:54.487
Here is a template you can copy.

69
00:03:54.767 --> 00:03:57.733
Hi Karan, thank you for the conversation yesterday.

70
00:03:58.013 --> 00:04:05.287
I enjoyed discussing the. event-driven. redesign of the order service, and it made me even more excited about the role.

71
00:04:05.567 --> 00:04:08.575
Please. let. me know if you need anything else from me.

72
00:04:08.855 --> 00:04:10.626
Looking forward to the next steps.

73
00:04:13.476 --> 00:04:15.567
No reply after the promised date.

74
00:04:15.847 --> 00:04:17.724
Here is a template you can copy.

75
00:04:18.004 --> 00:04:21.076
Hi Riya, just checking in on the final-round feedback.

76
00:04:21.356 --> 00:04:23.276
You'd mentioned we might hear. by.

77
00:04:23.556 --> 00:04:24.431
Friday.

78
00:04:24.711 --> 00:04:28.935
I have another process moving forward, so an update would really help me plan.

79
00:04:29.215 --> 00:04:30.068
Thank you!

80
00:04:32.918 --> 00:04:33.857
Part 6.

81
00:04:34.137 --> 00:04:35.374
Handling outcomes.

82
00:04:36.624 --> 00:04:37.989
Here is a quick table:

83
00:04:38.269 --> 00:04:40.061
Situation, and What to say.

84
00:04:40.341 --> 00:04:41.237
Rejection:

85
00:04:41.517 --> 00:04:42.968
Thank you for letting me know.

86
00:04:43.248 --> 00:04:45.936
Could you share any feedback that would help me improve?

87
00:04:46.216 --> 00:04:48.648
I'd be glad to be considered for future roles.

88
00:04:48.928 --> 00:04:49.995
Offer you want:

89
00:04:50.275 --> 00:04:52.109
Thank you, I'm really excited!

90
00:04:52.389 --> 00:04:55.931
Could you send the detailed offer so I can review the full package?

91
00:04:56.211 --> 00:04:58.152
(Then see Salary Negotiation.).

92
00:04:58.432 --> 00:04:59.648
Offer you'll decline:

93
00:04:59.928 --> 00:05:01.827
Thank you for the offer and your time.

94
00:05:02.107 --> 00:05:06.693
After careful thought, I've decided to accept another role that's a closer fit.

95
00:05:06.973 --> 00:05:08.637
I hope our paths cross again.

96
00:05:08.917 --> 00:05:09.963
Need more time:

97
00:05:10.243 --> 00:05:12.205
Could I have until Monday to decide?

98
00:05:12.485 --> 00:05:14.363
I want to make a careful decision.

99
00:05:14.643 --> 00:05:16.008
Joining date pushback:

100
00:05:16.288 --> 00:05:17.888
My notice is 60 days.

101
00:05:18.168 --> 00:05:21.923
I'll request an early release and can share an update in two weeks.

102
00:05:23.273 --> 00:05:24.211
Part 7.

103
00:05:24.491 --> 00:05:27.073
Conversation 1: recruiter screening call.

104
00:05:28.323 --> 00:05:30.349
Here is how the conversation goes.

105
00:05:30.629 --> 00:05:33.125
Hi Ashish, this is Riya from TalentBridge.

106
00:05:33.405 --> 00:05:35.219
Is this a good time to talk?

107
00:05:35.499 --> 00:05:38.656
Hi Riya, yes, I have about 15 minutes.

108
00:05:38.936 --> 00:05:39.875
Great.

109
00:05:40.155 --> 00:05:43.355
I'm hiring a Senior Backend Engineer for a fintech client.

110
00:05:43.635 --> 00:05:45.256
Are you open to a change?

111
00:05:45.536 --> 00:05:47.029
Yes, for the right role.

112
00:05:47.309 --> 00:05:50.275
Could you tell me a bit about the product and the team?

113
00:05:51.625 --> 00:05:53.225
The conversation continues.

114
00:05:53.505 --> 00:05:57.451
It's a payments platform team of eight people, mostly Java and Kafka.

115
00:05:57.731 --> 00:06:00.099
That's very relevant to my experience.

116
00:06:00.379 --> 00:06:02.406
What's the interview process like?

117
00:06:02.686 --> 00:06:06.825
A coding round, a system design round, a managerial round, and HR.

118
00:06:07.105 --> 00:06:08.769
Usually two to three weeks.

119
00:06:09.049 --> 00:06:10.798
And what's the budgeted range?

120
00:06:12.148 --> 00:06:13.748
The conversation continues.

121
00:06:14.028 --> 00:06:17.313
Up to 58 lakh rupees, depending on the interviews.

122
00:06:17.593 --> 00:06:19.172
What's your notice period?

123
00:06:19.452 --> 00:06:22.716
Sixty days, but it's negotiable to 45.

124
00:06:22.996 --> 00:06:24.041
Perfect.

125
00:06:24.321 --> 00:06:26.945
I'll share the JD and schedule the first round.

126
00:06:27.225 --> 00:06:28.164
Thank you.

127
00:06:28.444 --> 00:06:32.753
Please send the JD to my email, and I'll confirm a slot today.

128
00:06:34.103 --> 00:06:34.978
Part 8.

129
00:06:35.258 --> 00:06:38.778
Conversation 2: asking a former colleague for a referral.

130
00:06:40.028 --> 00:06:42.055
Here is how the conversation goes.

131
00:06:42.335 --> 00:06:43.593
Hi Arjun!

132
00:06:43.873 --> 00:06:45.217
It's been a while.

133
00:06:45.497 --> 00:06:47.332
How's life at Brightsoft?

134
00:06:47.612 --> 00:06:48.593
Hey Ashish!

135
00:06:48.873 --> 00:06:50.217
Really good, thanks.

136
00:06:50.497 --> 00:06:51.671
What's new with you?

137
00:06:51.951 --> 00:06:53.764
I'm exploring new roles.

138
00:06:54.044 --> 00:06:57.628
I saw that your team is hiring a senior backend engineer.

139
00:06:57.908 --> 00:06:59.785
Oh yes, we need people badly.

140
00:07:00.065 --> 00:07:01.324
Are you interested?

141
00:07:02.674 --> 00:07:04.274
The conversation continues.

142
00:07:04.554 --> 00:07:05.301
Very.

143
00:07:05.581 --> 00:07:07.714
Would you be comfortable referring me?

144
00:07:07.994 --> 00:07:11.109
I can send you my CV and a short summary.

145
00:07:11.389 --> 00:07:12.306
Of course.

146
00:07:12.586 --> 00:07:14.719
Send them over and I'll submit it today.

147
00:07:14.999 --> 00:07:16.365
Thank you so much.

148
00:07:16.645 --> 00:07:20.549
Is there anything about the team I should know before the interviews?

149
00:07:20.829 --> 00:07:24.199
They care a lot about system design and clear communication.

150
00:07:24.479 --> 00:07:25.546
You'll be fine!

151
00:07:26.896 --> 00:07:28.496
The conversation continues.

152
00:07:28.776 --> 00:07:30.205
That's really helpful.

153
00:07:30.485 --> 00:07:32.021
I owe you a coffee!

154
00:07:33.371 --> 00:07:34.267
Part 9.

155
00:07:34.547 --> 00:07:36.254
Weekly job-search routine.

156
00:07:37.504 --> 00:07:40.853
5 personalised referral or networking messages.

157
00:07:41.133 --> 00:07:45.016
5 to 10 targeted applications (not 50 random ones).

158
00:07:45.296 --> 00:07:48.389
2 mock interviews (with a friend or the master prompt).

159
00:07:48.669 --> 00:07:50.653
1 new STAR story written down.

160
00:07:50.933 --> 00:07:55.435
Update a simple tracker: company, role, contact, stage, next step, date.

161
00:07:56.785 --> 00:07:57.638
Part 10.

162
00:07:57.918 --> 00:07:58.963
Speak today.

163
00:08:00.213 --> 00:08:04.693
Write your answer to Why are you looking for a change? in one positive sentence.

164
00:08:04.973 --> 00:08:07.085
Draft one referral request message.

165
00:08:07.365 --> 00:08:12.016
Practise saying your expected CTC and notice period out loud, calmly.

166
00:08:13.366 --> 00:08:14.902
That's the end of this lesson.

167
00:08:15.182 --> 00:08:19.854
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

168
00:08:20.134 --> 00:08:26.235
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

